prompts.expectations_review:
Review the fairness of an existing benchmark scenario set before it is used for a NEW comparison. The set is plugins/developing-ai-agents/evals/benchmark-v3.json in /home/ikruglov/developing-ai-agents-skill: 32 scenarios, 26 free-form answers and 6 filled artifacts.

It was built to compare two versions of the same skill. Now it will compare the answer of the current skill 0.7.3 against the answer of the same model with no skill at all. Both arms get identical prompts and the same attached fixtures, and neither may open other files.

Read the skill for reference: plugins/developing-ai-agents/skills/developing-ai-agents/SKILL.md, plus references/templates/ and references/playbooks/.

You are read-only. Do not dispatch subagents.

For every expectation, decide whether a strong engineer who never saw this skill, but knows the field and the book's ideas, could satisfy it from the prompt and fixtures alone. Flag expectations that grade any of these instead of engineering substance:
- the skill's own vocabulary, template field names or section headings;
- file or command names;
- the required order of sections;
- labels such as «evidence/inference/unknown».

Also flag:
- composite expectations that bundle 3 or more claims;
- expectations that are unanswerable from the prompt;
- expectations the prompt does not ask for.

For each flagged expectation, propose a rewrite that keeps the engineering substance, can be graded by meaning in any wording, and is a single checkable claim. Keep 3–5 expectations per scenario. Do not change the prompts.

Write the result as a JSON file at /home/ikruglov/developing-ai-agents-skill/.tmp/bench-v6/expectations-fair.json. Format:
{"<id>": {"expectations": [ ...final list... ], "changed": [indices], "why": {"<index>": "reason"}}}
Include every scenario, including unchanged ones with "changed": []. Write nothing else in the repo.

Reply with: how many expectations changed out of the total, the ids of the artifact scenarios, and whether the artifact scenarios needed changes.
